# intent-longbox environment — copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit real values.
# Real secrets live in SOPS-encrypted files per the estate standard; this file
# documents the variable NAMES only.

# --- Core ---
# THE VALUES BELOW ARE THE LOCAL DEV STACK, NOT PLACEHOLDERS (E02-B10). They point
# at `docker compose -f docker-compose.test.yml up -d`: port 54329 (not 5432, which
# nothing in this repo ever listens on), database `longbox` (created by
# docker/postgres-init/01-dev-database.sql), and the throwaway role passwords from
# docker/postgres-init/00-roles.sql. Those passwords ARE NOT SECRETS and must never
# become one — the container is bound to 127.0.0.1 for the test lane. Production
# roles are provisioned by the deploy contract with passwords held in SOPS.
# Until this bead the file documented port 5432 and a database nothing created, so
# `pnpm migrate` against a fresh checkout failed twice over.
#
# TWO Postgres URLs, deliberately different roles (E02-D06, 041 §9.2 item 2).
#
# DATABASE_URL is the APPLICATION role. It owns no table and is not a superuser,
# so it cannot `SET session_replication_role` and cannot
# `ALTER TABLE … DISABLE TRIGGER` — which is what makes the append-only guarantee
# (locked decision 4) something the database enforces rather than something the
# server promises. The server asserts this at boot and refuses to serve if the
# role it connects as owns any append-only table.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://longbox_app:longbox_app@127.0.0.1:54329/longbox
# MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL is the SCHEMA-OWNING role. `pnpm migrate`,
# `pnpm grant-app-role` and `pnpm register-shop` use it; nothing serving HTTP does.
# Unset in a non-production shell it falls back to DATABASE_URL with a loud
# warning; with NODE_ENV=production the fallback is refused.
MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://longbox_migrate:longbox_migrate@127.0.0.1:54329/longbox
# Optional: the app role's NAME, when a deployment does not call it longbox_app.
# Read by the grant step only; passwords never appear here (values live in SOPS).
# APP_DB_ROLE=longbox_app
# HTTP listen port
PORT=3000
# Directory for uploaded scan photos (v0: local disk)
UPLOADS_DIR=uploads

# --- LLM providers (BYOK) ---
# Default provider key (Anthropic / Claude is the default and reference provider)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Pinned default vision model
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# OpenAI-compatible provider (optional alternative adapter)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Generic gateway override (jrig Transport lore) — when set, WINS over the
# per-provider settings above and routes the active adapter through it.
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# Confidence band thresholds (0..1). high >= BAND_HIGH, medium >= BAND_MEDIUM, else low.
BAND_HIGH=0.85
BAND_MEDIUM=0.5

# --- Pricing (dual sources: PriceCharting historical FMV + eBay live asks) ---
# PriceCharting API token (Premium). Empty = stub client (no live comps).
PRICECHARTING_TOKEN=
# eBay Browse API app credentials (OAuth2 client-credentials; the app token is
# fetched and cached automatically). BOTH empty = stub client (no live asks).
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional: sandbox host (default https://api.ebay.com) and category filter
# (default 259104 = Comics & Graphic Novels).
# EBAY_BASE_URL=https://api.sandbox.ebay.com

# --- Shopify (per-store Dev Dashboard app for the pilot) ---
# Empty = stub client (no live drafts). Admin API access token, store domain,
# pinned API version.
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=
SHOPIFY_ADMIN_TOKEN=
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2025-07

# --- Outbox drain (E02-D07, 043 §5.3, §7.1) ---
# FOUR PROVISIONAL FLOORS AND ONE INTERVAL. These are NOT measurements, are
# never quoted as reliability, throughput or latency in any artifact at any
# class (021 B16), and support no claim of fact. They are circuit-breaker
# floors adopted under 042 A3 ("018 A3 caps claims of fact, not safety
# floors"). They close by measurement across the 019 §5 pilot batches,
# SEGMENTED by whether a real Shopify credential was configured — a stub client
# never fails, so a mixed sample would report a reliability belonging to the
# stub. 018 C3's red line: a ceiling may be RAISED freely because it binds
# less; LOWERING one after seeing a result it would change needs a 006 row.
# Unset everywhere = the defaults in src/services/outbox.ts.
# OUTBOX_MAX_ATTEMPTS=6
# OUTBOX_BACKOFF_BASE_MS=30000
# OUTBOX_BACKOFF_CEILING_MS=1800000
# ATTEMPT VISIBILITY: the in-flight window. ⚠ It must exceed the worst-case
# CLOCK SKEW across every host that runs a worker (043 A7) — every timestamp in
# the design is server-side now(), and beyond a single host NTP or a monotonic
# source is a requirement, not an operational nicety.
# OUTBOX_ATTEMPT_VISIBILITY_MS=300000
# OUTBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5000
# OUTBOX_BATCH_SIZE=10

# --- Shopify dev-store upsert-consistency check (A11, OPEN) ---
# 043 A11 signs ONE assumption OPEN: that a `customId` written by a productSet
# CREATE is immediately findable by a productSet upsert issued moments later. A
# metafield-backed lookup that were eventually consistent would make a fast
# retry create a SECOND product — the exact failure the key exists to prevent —
# and no citation can settle it, because the question is about behaviour and
# not documentation. It closes by MEASUREMENT against an ISOLATED DEV STORE,
# before the saga serves a real shop.
#
# Set all three and run `pnpm test:integration` to execute
# tests/integration/shopify-customid-consistency.test.ts; it SKIPS otherwise.
# ⚠ NEVER point these at a live shop: the test creates a real product.
# SHOPIFY_DEV_STORE_DOMAIN=
# SHOPIFY_DEV_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# SHOPIFY_DEV_API_VERSION=2025-07

# --- Per-shop credential overrides (BYOK seam) ---
# shop_credentials.key_ref stores the NAME of an env var, never a raw key.
# Example: register-shop creates key_ref "SHOP_GOTHAM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"; you
# then export that variable here. When a shop has no credential row for a kind,
# resolution falls back to the global vars above.
# SHOP_GOTHAM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# SHOP_GOTHAM_SHOPIFY_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# SHOP_GOTHAM_PRICECHARTING_TOKEN=
# eBay is a credential PAIR: the key_ref names the client-ID var; the secret
# lives at `${key_ref}_SECRET` (still names-in-DB, raw keys only in env/SOPS).
# SHOP_GOTHAM_EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
# SHOP_GOTHAM_EBAY_CLIENT_ID_SECRET=
